lung|breathing-organ|NOUN|organ used in breathing|One of the organs in the chest that take air into the body during breathing.|phổi|The diagram shows the position of each lung inside the chest.|Sơ đồ cho thấy vị trí của từng lá phổi bên trong lồng ngực.|Countable: a lung, two lungs. Often plural when discussing breathing.|0
reportedly|according-to-reports|ADVERB|according to reports|According to information that has been reported, though not confirmed by the speaker.|theo nguồn tin; được cho là|The missing statue was reportedly found in a private collection.|Theo nguồn tin, bức tượng bị mất đã được tìm thấy trong một bộ sưu tập tư nhân.|Sentence adverb; reportedly does not establish that a report is true. Often used in news writing.|0
statute|enacted-written-law|NOUN|formally enacted written law|A written law formally passed by a body with lawmaking authority.|đạo luật|The fictional council debated a proposal to revise an old statute.|Hội đồng trong truyện tranh luận về đề xuất sửa đổi một đạo luật cũ.|Countable; a statute, statutes; under a statute. A statute is not a statue.|-
warning|notice-of-danger|NOUN|notice of possible danger|A message or sign that alerts someone to possible danger or trouble.|lời cảnh báo; dấu hiệu cảnh báo|The flashing light gave a warning that the battery was nearly empty.|Đèn nhấp nháy báo hiệu rằng pin sắp cạn.|Countable: a warning about something, a warning of danger. A warning can be a signal rather than spoken words.|0
carriage|railway-passenger-car|NOUN|passenger part of a train|A railway vehicle in which passengers travel.|toa tàu chở khách|Our seats were in the last carriage of the morning train.|Chỗ ngồi của chúng tôi ở toa cuối của chuyến tàu buổi sáng.|Countable; railway carriage is common in British English; car is common in American English.|0
carriage|horse-drawn-vehicle|NOUN|horse-drawn passenger vehicle|A vehicle pulled by horses and used to carry people.|xe ngựa chở người|The restored carriage stood beside a photograph of its former owner.|Chiếc xe ngựa đã được phục chế nằm cạnh ảnh của người chủ trước đây.|Countable; a horse-drawn carriage. Distinct from a railway carriage.|1
